---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/10-14/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="10-14 · dry display fixture" description="Inspect an original dry fixture, the fit of a solid rectangular display block, and detached tag labels. No physiological simulation." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment df"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/10-14/">← Equipment 10-14</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#df-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">10-14 · DRY VISUALIZATION ONLY / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Dry fixture display</h2><p>This is a non-operational visual placeholder for Equipment 10-14. Check how a solid rectangular prop fits a fixed mount, and compare detached tags against the drawing.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Original metric mockup</h3><div id="df-view" aria-label="Orbitable dry rectangular display with a solid block, clear cover walls and separate dummy tag rack"></div><div class="bar"><button data-df-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-df-view="mount">Dry mount close-up</button><button data-df-view="tags">Detached tags</button></div><p id="df-ready" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. Click either teal badge to show or hide the display block or labels. Nothing can be connected or energized.</p></section>
<section><h3>Inert fit and label check</h3><canvas width="700" height="330" id="df-diagram" aria-label="Top view of the rectangular block and mount, with a separate left and right tag display"></canvas><div class="fields"><label>Block X offset (mm)<input id="df-xMm" type="number" step="any" min="-45" max="45" value="0"/></label><label>Block Y offset (mm)<input id="df-yMm" type="number" step="any" min="-45" max="45" value="0"/></label><label>Left tag<select id="df-leftTag"><option selected value="TAG-A">TAG-A</option><option value="TAG-B">TAG-B</option></select></label><label>Right tag<select id="df-rightTag"><option value="TAG-A">TAG-A</option><option selected value="TAG-B">TAG-B</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="df-inspect">Inspect mockup</button><button id="df-insert">Hide display block</button><button id="df-tags">Hide tag labels</button><button id="df-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="df-status" aria-live="polite">Inspect the centered block, then try a 12 mm X offset or change either label.</p><output id="df-result">No inspection report yet.</output><button id="df-export" disabled>Export inspection JSON</button></section></div>
<section id="df-evidence"><h3>Design and evidence</h3><p>Original design R1. Exterior dimensions and component sizes are nominal design choices, not measurements of a manufacturer unit. Geometry uses the <a href="https://registry.khronos.org/glTF/specs/2.0/glTF-2.0.html#coordinate-system-and-units">glTF 2.0 meter scale</a>; planar inspection coordinates are labeled in millimeters. No equipment photos are claimed for this custom dry placeholder.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original 3D rendering of the dry rectangular display and physically separate tag rack"/><figcaption>Original perspective, not a photograph. The tag rack is physically separate and carries only capped, disconnected visual props.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'plan.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original top render showing fixed recess rails and inert rectangular insert"/><figcaption>Original plan view. All clearances refer to the authored rectangular geometry.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Reference</th><th>Actual / meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Base width × depth / dry recess</td><td>410 × 220 mm; 85 × 120 mm nominal</td><td>Metric model matches the original design, not measured hardware.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Centered prop</td><td>Solid 65 × 80 mm footprint</td><td>10 mm each side and 20 mm front/back; analytical tolerance 10⁻¹² mm.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Shift X by +12 mm</td><td>−2 mm right margin</td><td>Interference flagged; zero marks exact contact.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tag arrangement</td><td>TAG-A left, TAG-B right</td><td>Other order flagged. This is a visual label comparison, not a connectivity test.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Register physiological test</td><td>Propagation latency and separation</td><td>Not implemented or run. No actual specimen, fluid, stimulation, recordings, or physiology are included.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>For each axis, subtract the solid prop size from the recess size and divide by two. One offset increases a margin and reduces the opposite one. The labels are compared as text only; all props stay power-disconnected. The export records exact design IDs, offsets, nominal fit margins, visible tags and revisions.</p>
<p><a href={base+'dry-fixture.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'example-report.json'}>Output example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or hardware validation claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/10-14/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.df{max-width:76rem}.df .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.df section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.df .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.df .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.df label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.df input,.df select,.df button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.df button{cursor:pointer}.df button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.df .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.df #df-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.df #df-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.df #df-diagram,.df img{width:100%;height:auto}.df #df-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.df #df-status.error{color:#a54a34}.df .scroll{overflow:auto}.df table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.df td,.df th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.df figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.df .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
